  "instruction": "Complete the implementation of `glom.matching._precedence(pattern)` so that pattern-matching specifications in dictionaries and structured specifiers (such as `Match`, `Check`, `Switch`, `Regex`, and logical combinators like `And`, `Or`, `Not`) evaluate candidate spec keys in the correct priority order.\n\nWhen a target key can match multiple spec keys (for example, the target `1` matching a literal `1`, type `int`, and predicate `M > 0`), `_precedence` must return an ordering score where lower values correspond to higher priority (tried earlier) and higher values correspond to lower priority (tried later).\n\nThe ordering must properly distinguish between literal exact values, specialized patterns/types/predicates, wrapped/nested combinators (e.g., `And`, `Or`, `Not`), and broad catch-all or fallback matchers, ensuring double-wrapped patterns, nested structures, and sample matching test suites pass consistently.",
